{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"The strongest story is finite-horizon non-generalization, with a censoring audit. I’ll now write the strategy and figure specifications.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/home/agent-home/.codex/tmp/arg0/codex-arg01Wi7zG/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Memorization Without Observed Grokking Across MLP Widths\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"Within a fixed training horizon, how do hidden width and weight decay affect memorization and observed generalization in modular-arithmetic MLPs, and what can a censored width-lag contrast actually establish?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"Across the tested modular addition and subtraction conditions, wider fixed-rate MLPs attain sustained memorization earlier or attain it when the narrowest models do not, yet none attains sustained generalization within 20,000 updates; the reported width-lag contrast therefore reflects memorization and endpoint substitution, not an identified effect on grokking time.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The final evidence supports a controlled, finite-horizon negative-results study across width and decay, augmented by an exact audit of the reported lag statistic. This is stronger than a proposed capacity-versus-decay-clock mechanism, which lacks the proposed random-label and calibration interventions, or a learning-rate-superiority story, which lacks a final-plane comparator. The scientific contribution is the observed separation between fitting and generalization plus the identification limit of capped lag, not a new optimizer or a universal claim about model scale. The original mechanistic question is only partially answered. Negative results support a coherent standalone paper, but readiness is not a prediction of ICLR acceptance.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"Fresh framing rather than an edit: no previous_paper directory, resolved edit-context files, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory is present. The status recentered refers to replacing the source proposal's mechanistic ambition with the actually evaluated finite-horizon question; it does not imply that a prior manuscript existed. Preserve-proposal, broaden-to-annealing-family, and recenter-on-final-factorial framings were compared; the last has the strongest directly observed evidence.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"No staged old/new manuscript or implementation pair is available, so no inherited title, central question, or figure plan is retained by inertia.\\\",\n+    \\\"The hash-matched final evaluator fixes the actual setting: modulus 97, addition and subtraction, concatenated one-hot inputs, one-hidden-layer ReLU MLPs of widths 16, 64, and 256, full-batch AdamW, weight decay 0 or 1, and a 20,000-update horizon.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final evidence contains three seed episodes, each with twelve factorial condition records: 36 completed training records, 30 sustained memorization events, and zero sustained generalization events. These are deterministic summaries of final.evidence.episodes, not search outcomes.\\\",\n+    \\\"The available constant-rate implementation specifies learning rate 0.01. Its linkage to the final evaluation is supported by the retained implementation and campaign manifest; the final manifest supplies a program-tree hash but not an independently verified reconstructed source tree. Do not claim stronger file-level provenance than this.\\\",\n+    \\\"downstream_study is absent and there are no study.* grounding sources. Do not create a search-selection table, score-difference claim, or scored/unscored attempt accounting from memory or substitute result.* sources for a study contract.\\\",\n+    \\\"Final qualification is independently recorded as status completed, outcome qualified, and correct true by final.qualification.*. This does not establish scientific validity, adaptivity safeguards, superiority, or a grokking mechanism. Candidate diagnostic trust is labeled unverified; scientific observations here are the retained evaluator-generated traces, not candidate self-reports.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Fixed-rate MLP width family without weight decay\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Widths 16, 64, and 256 at the frozen constant-rate recipe supply the within-final-evaluation reference for fitting times and held-out behavior in both operations. This is a scientific reference condition, not an unevaluated original-program comparison.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Matched width family with unit weight decay\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The same widths, operation-specific data, seed values, training horizon, and learning-rate recipe with AdamW decay 1 isolate the evaluated decay intervention conditional on this architecture and initialization scheme. The narrowest networks never attain the memorization threshold, unlike widths 64 and 256.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Nonlearning prediction references\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Stored initial-network, training-label-mode, exact-pair lookup with mode fallback, and label-deranged-input prediction accuracies contextualize low held-out accuracy. The lookup and mode references coincide because held-out pairs are disjoint. These are not separately trained random-label networks and are not a causal mechanism test.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Lead with a width-by-decay comparison, split by addition and subtraction, rather than learning-rate search order. Use late-window training and held-out accuracy with individual seed observations; both operations are evidence blocks for one finite-horizon thesis, not separate discoveries.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep a main-text event table for all twelve operation/decay/width cells. Report all three observed memorization times or non-attainment, alongside generalization attainment counts. Widths 64 and 256 memorize at checkpoint 500 in every condition; width 16 without decay memorizes at 1000 or 1500; width 16 with decay never crosses. All 36 generalization events are unobserved.\\\",\n+    \\\"Define memorization as training accuracy at least 0.99 and generalization as held-out accuracy at least 0.95 at three consecutive checkpoints. Checkpoints are 500 updates apart; event times are the first checkpoint of a qualifying triplet, not precisely resolved continuous crossing times. Delayed generalization requires both observed events and a positive lag.\\\",\n+    \\\"Audit the capped-lag statistic explicitly. Its value is T when memorization is absent and max(0, (G if observed else T) - M) otherwise. For positive decay, the narrowest models receive T and width-256 models receive T-500, mechanically giving the reported 500-update contrast and [500, 500] interval. Report that interval faithfully as the supplied three-seed statistic, not as precision about unobserved generalization times.\\\",\n+    \\\"The supplied decay interaction of 1083.3333333333335 updates is also an interaction of the capped statistic, not evidence that decay changes a generalization clock. The negative no-decay width contrast follows earlier memorization in larger networks while generalization is absent. Keep the algebra and the censoring caveat in the main paper.\\\",\n+    \\\"Contextualize final held-out accuracy using stored nonlearning references. If the aggregate final accuracy or control gap is reported, define it in reader-facing units: the final-five-checkpoint mean and the equally weighted gap to four references, respectively. Do not treat the aggregate as superiority or compare it to search-plane aggregates.\\\",\n+    \\\"Show seed values rather than relying on significance tests. There are three independent initialization seeds on a fixed split per operation; the twelve condition records within a seed are paired, not twelve independent replications. Zero observed generalization does not identify eventual event rates or support a pooled independent-binomial confidence interval.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: the evaluated width-by-decay design, distinct memorization/generalization events, and the inference boundary imposed by a finite horizon. No invented learning curves or proposed unrun interventions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, main comparison: a 2-by-2 quantitative display of late-window training and held-out accuracy against width; columns are operations, rows are distinct accuracy metrics, colors encode decay, and seed points remain visible.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, censoring audit: two direct-comparison panels, one per decay condition, showing capped lag versus width with operation-specific series and individual seeds. Explicitly label every generalization time as unobserved and explain the endpoint-substitution identity next to the figure.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"study_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the evaluated factorial design and the difference between fitting, generalization, and censoring legible at a glance without asserting a neural mechanism.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"evaluated_factor_and_event_definition\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"not_applicable_design_schematic\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"design_and_inference_boundary\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected ICLR style has one 5.5-inch text column, not a two-column layout. Two adjacent schematic compartments need the entire 5.5-inch width; a nominal half-width rendering would be only 2.75 inches and force tiny labels. Target 1.7-2.0 inches of graphic height plus caption, about 0.3 body page, on page 1 or 2.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"minimum_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Left: addition/subtraction mod 97; three widths; decay 0/1; three seeds; one shared fixed-rate MLP protocol. Right: separate named memorization and generalization event definitions, the 20,000-update observation limit, and an explicit distinction between non-attainment and measured delay. Use grouping labels instead of twelve tiny condition boxes. Draw no synthetic trajectories, causal circuit arrows, or additional unperformed experiments.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"export_requirements\\\": \\\"Retain editable draw.io source and vector PDF export when available, plus a PNG generated at the required resolution. Reference the PDF in LaTeX whenever a PDF exists; if only raster survives, require at least 2400 pixels width, generated from source rather than upscaled.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"width_decay_outcomes\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Compare fitting and held-out behavior directly across widths and decay while displaying all seed-level uncertainty.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"faceted_seed_dotplot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"hidden_width\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"mean_accuracy_over_final_five_checkpoints\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"operation_and_accuracy_partition\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Four panels in two rows and two columns fit the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width at approximately 2.5 inches per panel after gutters. Target 3.1-3.5 inches graphic height plus caption, about 0.45 body page. Separate row scales prevent near-zero held-out values from disappearing under the training-accuracy range; scales match across operations within each row. Do not shrink a four-panel figure to half text width.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"minimum_rendered_font_pt\\\": 8.5,\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Columns: addition and subtraction. Top row: training accuracy averaged over each trace's last five checkpoints. Bottom row: held-out accuracy over that same window, matching each record's stored score. Plot widths 16, 64, 256 as categorical positions; use two consistent decay colors and three seed markers per condition with deterministic offsets. Show seed means without fabricated error bars. Do not label a single series as successful or reuse one threshold label across the two accuracy definitions. The main event table supplies sustained-threshold results.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"export_requirements\\\": \\\"Generate PDF and PNG from the same plotting script, PNG at 300 DPI and at least 2400 pixels wide; keep the PDF vector and reference it in LaTeX. Regenerate with appropriate source dimensions rather than upscaling a raster.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"censoring_audit\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose why a nonzero capped-lag width contrast is compatible with zero observed generalization events.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"faceted_capped_lag_dotplot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"hidden_width\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"administratively_capped_lag_in_updates\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"weight_decay\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Two side-by-side panels need the full 5.5-inch text width so capped observations, a shared legend, and the non-attainment annotation remain legible at 9-point text. Target 2.0-2.3 inches graphic height plus caption, about 0.3 body page. Use a visibly labeled focused vertical range covering the observed capped values; never imply a zero origin or an observed event at the cap.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"minimum_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Panels: decay 0 and decay 1. Two series encode operation using a separate, clearly labeled visual role from Figure 2's decay colors; prefer neutral operation-specific shapes/line patterns to avoid color reassignment. Draw each seed's capped lag and a condition mean. Distinguish missing memorization from observed memorization by fill or an explicit annotation. All generalization events are unobserved. Include the capped-lag formula in adjacent main text and report the 500-update contrast with its supplied degenerate interval there. Width is the horizontal axis, not search order or training progression.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_contrast\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.metric.decay_interaction\\\"],\n+      \\\"export_requirements\\\": \\\"Generate vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG from one script, PNG at least 2400 pixels wide. LaTeX must use the PDF whenever present. Preserve visible capped-data symbols and readable annotations at the final 5.5-inch width.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Provide an auditable condition-level record, exact data and training specification, and substantive reference-predictor and diagnostic detail without relocating the negative result or the censoring explanation out of the main paper.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Exact Data and Training Specification\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the actual modulus-97 dataset construction, deterministic operation-specific split, and final-plane pool: 4705 pairs per operation, 1411 training and 3294 held-out. Specify one-hot concatenation, linear-ReLU-linear architecture, parameter counts 4769/18785/74849, full-batch cross-entropy, AdamW defaults explicitly set by the evaluator, checkpoint cadence, constant learning-rate implementation, and seeds 1009/2027/3037. Architectural and split facts come from the hash-matched task/evaluate_final.py and task/resources/final/benchmark.json; episode records anchor the evaluated cases and measured parameter counts. Do not replace these with proposal-only settings.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Condition-Level Observations\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Give a 36-row seed/operation/decay/width table with memorization event or non-attainment, generalization non-attainment, capped lag, final-five-checkpoint training and held-out accuracy, and completion status. Retain every condition, including the six narrow positive-decay fitting failures and all zero generalization outcomes. The main paper retains the twelve-cell event summary and decisive comparisons.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.completion_fraction\\\", \\\"final.metric.delayed_fraction\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Reference Predictors and Available Diagnostics\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate each stored reference accuracy separately rather than only the aggregate control gap. Explain the duplicate lookup/mode reference and the held-out-label construction of the deranged-input diagnostic. Provide condition-level endpoint loss and weight-norm summaries from the existing traces only; mark them descriptive and avoid circuit, representation, or causal explanations. No new random-label training, calibration intervention, or norm ablation is implied.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_gap\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Capped-Lag Calculation and Reproduction Map\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Supply exact event and aggregation pseudocode from the hash-matched final evaluator, the paired-by-seed contrast calculation and its Student-t multiplier, derivations of every reported aggregate, and an artifact-to-script/table/figure map. Keep the central 500-update identity and its scientific limitation in the body. Reproduction instructions must distinguish training from replotting stored results, list numpy 2.1.3 and torch 2.5.1+cpu from task/requirements.txt, and describe the actual RPC dependency rather than inventing a standalone command. Omit unmeasured runtime estimates and unverified hardware claims.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.restricted_mean_lag\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_contrast\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.metric.decay_interaction\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the artifact-supported roles of LLMs in idea proposal, the bounded learning-rate implementation, reference-query planning, and paper framing/writing. Distinguish evaluator-owned neural training and measurements from generated prose and candidate proposals. State only observed roles; do not infer undocumented human review or model identities. Relevant implementation files and reference_query_plan.md provide provenance in addition to the final evidence record.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Campaign Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Search Timeline\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Successful Run\\\",\n+    \\\"Phase 1 / Phase 2\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Configuration\\\",\n+    \\\"Successive Improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"Capacity-versus-Decay-Clock Mechanism Confirmed\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"search winner proves\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"larger models grok faster\\\",\n+    \\\"grokking never occurs\\\",\n+    \\\"the confidence interval proves faster generalization\\\",\n+    \\\"random-label control experiments\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"PUBLIC OUTLINE AND PAGE PLAN: Target 8.5 body pages under VENUE.md, within its 8-9-page requirement and without changing the template geometry. Allocate approximately 1.5 pages to abstract/introduction and the early overview, 0.75 to related work, 1.75 to methods and event definitions, 3.0 to results including both quantitative figures and the twelve-cell event table, 1.25 to discussion/limitations, and 0.25 to conclusion. These are layout budgets, not measurements. Ensure an eight-page body ends at least 75% full. Use available space for the event/censoring derivation, transparent references, paired uncertainty, and scope analysis rather than additional weak claims. If this cannot fill the budget substantively, flag that conflict rather than add filler.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC SECTION PLAN: Introduction; Related Work; Experimental Design and Event Definitions; Results with Width and Decay Effects on Fitting, Held-Out Outcomes, and What the Capped Lag Measures; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. After references, begin Supplementary Information with the planned grounded subsections, including a separate LLM Usage section. No visible search chronology.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC HYPOTHESIS PLAN: Present the modest accounting explanation that finite-horizon width differences in fitting can generate apparent lag differences without observed differences in generalization. State testable implications for the stored event table and the exact capped-lag identity, and label this interpretation retrospective, not preregistered. The data support earlier fitting at larger widths but cannot test the original equivalence prediction about true generalization times, a capacity mechanism, or a decay-clock explanation. New generalization events or a failure of the identity would defeat the present account of these observed contrasts.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC UNCERTAINTY PLAN: Report individual initialization seeds, fixed data splits, pairing, and checkpoint resolution. A first sustained event requires a triplet, so late threshold excursions lacking two following observations cannot qualify. Administrative non-attainment is not evidence of permanent failure. Do not impute unobserved event times as actual times or fit a survival curve that purports to estimate an unseen generalization-time distribution. In narrow positive-decay cases, a post-memorization lag is undefined; the value T is a scoring convention.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC LIMITATIONS: One modulus, two related operations, one representation and one-hidden-layer architecture, three widths, three initializations, a fixed split per operation, only two decay values, one selected learning-rate recipe, no scale-matched initialization, no random-label training control, no mechanistic circuit measures, and a finite horizon. Checkpoint ties do not establish identical continuous-time dynamics. Decay changes the trained system; norms alone cannot attribute a mechanism. Original broader scientific predictions remain untested.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC REFERENCE PLAN: Use only exact starter-literature identities verified against references.bib and references_provenance.json and actually consulted before substantive citation. Retrieval provenance includes off-target metadata and is not itself evidence that a work was read. Do not use query-string matches as paper-identity verification, expand citation graphs, or search broadly for width-grokking work. Stop and log any identifiable prohibited encounter. No external retrieval was performed during strategy generation; this stage inspected local reference metadata only. Use established grokking/AdamW context without claiming novelty by absence of a literature search.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC TEMPLATE PLAN: The inspected templates/iclr/paper.tex and paper.sty are single-column, with textwidth 5.5 inches and textheight 9 inches. The scaffold contains a named author and a final-copy command inconsistent with the brief's anonymous submission; the writer must use anonymous review mode, omit author affiliations/acknowledgements/funding and identifying links, preserve the required orchestrator watermark, and not change margins or fonts. Inspect ICLR 2026 compliance and any required checklist without inventing a checklist or claiming that the old style-file header independently certifies latest-template provenance.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC FIGURE PLAN: All required figures are full text width in this single-column format. Create only one concept figure through the specified orchestrator workflow; do not invoke it during strategy generation. Plan vector-first quantitative figures and retain editable sources. Export quantitative PDFs plus 300-DPI PNGs; at 5.5-inch final placement, obtain the required 2400-pixel PNG width by rendering the source canvas sufficiently large with proportionally scaled typography, not by raster upscaling. Prefer PDF in LaTeX whenever available. Raster-only assets require at least 2400 pixels full width or 1200 pixels column/partial width. Keep every required figure within its panel, category, series, and font budgets.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC MAIN-TEXT TABLE PLAN: Include a compact twelve-row event table, grouped by operation and decay, with width, the three seed-specific memorization times or non-attainment, and observed generalization count. Separately summarize nonlearning-reference definitions and their equality where appropriate. Do not merge the 99% fitting threshold and 95% generalization threshold under an ambiguous successful-run label.\\\",\n+    \\\"PRIVATE-ONLY GROUNDING: Quantitative scientific sources are final.evidence.episodes and final.metric.*. Qualification must be read independently from final.qualification.status, final.qualification.outcome, and final.qualification.correct; current values are completed, qualified, and true. State the recorded evaluation outcome faithfully in the reproducibility disclosure as a completed evaluation accepted under its recorded criteria, while explicitly denying that acceptance certifies generalization or mechanism. If a revision changes the authoritative outcome to not_qualified, explicitly disclose failed qualification in the paper, review, audit, and revision; retain measurements with all limitations and do not diagnose performance, validity, or adaptivity failure without evaluator evidence. Missing gate diagnostics remain unknown. Keep pipeline-native field names and internal paths out of public prose.\\\",\n+    \\\"PRIVATE-ONLY SELECTION BOUNDARY: There is no downstream_study or study.* source namespace in this bundle. The implemented constant-rate policy is the studied fixed configuration, not a new inferred winner. The original source policy uses learning rate 0.001, but no comparable final-plane evaluation of it is retained; omit that empirical comparison rather than substitute search scores. Do not report search deltas, search winner claims, or scored/unscored attempt counts. Neither missing results nor discarded proposals are measured losses.\\\",\n+    \\\"PRIVATE-ONLY TRUST AND PROVENANCE: task/evaluate_final.py and ../final_evaluation/results/evaluation_evidence.json match the evaluator/evidence hashes in final metadata. The episode source is tagged candidate_diagnostics_trust unverified; it contains evaluator-generated training observations and must not be upgraded into a claim of comprehensive integrity/adaptivity certification. Supplement source_ids identify the existing episode registry entry; code and resource files named in grounded_content provide additional method provenance, not newly fabricated grounding IDs. No actual paper, figures, claim map, or final-paper validation should be produced in this strategy stage.\\\",\n+    \\\"SUPPLEMENT ROUTING: Keep the zero-generalization result, the narrow positive-decay fitting failure, all main event definitions, and the capped-lag caveat in the body. Place full seed tables, detailed data construction, predictor diagnostics, and reproduction mapping after references. Route any separately supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses to Supplementary Information without inventing rankings or modifying this strategy to guess them.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Strategy\n+\n+**Status:** ready for \"'`paper_standalone` using `write-paper-standalone`; strategy only, not a manuscript.\n+\n+**Provisional title:** Memorization Without Observed Grokking Across MLP Widths\n+\n+## Central Question and Thesis\n+\n+**Question.** Within a fixed training horizon, how do hidden width and weight decay affect memorization and observed generalization in modular-arithmetic MLPs, and what can a censored width-lag contrast actually establish?\n+\n+**Thesis.** Across the tested addition and subtraction conditions, wider fixed-rate MLPs attain sustained memorization earlier or attain it when the narrowest models do not. None attains sustained generalization within 20,000 updates. The reported width-lag contrast consequently reflects fitting and endpoint substitution, not an identified effect on grokking time.\n+\n+This is a finite-horizon negative-results paper with a metric-identification analysis, not a new scheduling algorithm or a demonstrated neural mechanism. Its strength is a clear separation between what the experiments observe and what their lag statistic cannot establish. It partially answers the original research question; it does not complete the original proposed mechanistic investigation. Readiness means a coherent grounded paper is possible, not that ICLR acceptance or a novelty claim has been established.\n+\n+## Evidence and Framing Decision\n+\n+No prior manuscript, resolved edit-context input, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` directory is present. The JSON status `recentered` describes a fresh shift from the source proposal to the observed scientific setting, not an edit to an existing paper. No inherited title or figure plan exists to preserve.\n+\n+Three framings were compared:\n+\n+| Candidate framing | Decision | Grounded reason |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Preserve the proposed capacity-versus-decay-clock explanation | Reject as the thesis | Random-label fitting controls, initial-logit calibration, and the proposed generalization-time equivalence test were not performed. |\n+| Broaden into an annealing or optimizer-method family | Reject as the thesis | A selected fixed recipe has final evidence, but alternate schedules and the original lower-rate implementation lack matched final-plane comparisons. Search scores cannot establish final superiority or a width mechanism. |\n+| Recenter on the final width-by-decay factorial and censoring boundary | Select | The final evaluator supplies all condition-level training traces and the event/aggregation definitions needed to explain the negative result and audit the lag contrast. |\n+\n+The final evidence is independent of the source proposals and recent memory. `downstream_study` is absent; no `study.*` grounding sources are supplied. Do not invent a campaign selection contract, search score differences, or scored/unscored attempt counts. Omit a comparison against the original learning-rate-0.001 implementation because no comparable final-plane result is retained. Missing performance evidence is not a loss.\n+\n+### Private Qualification and Provenance Audit\n+\n+The authoritative `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, and `final.qualification.correct` values are **completed**, **qualified**, and **true**, respectively. Do not replace these with an earlier search acceptance or failure label. Record the completed, accepted evaluation in a reader-facing reproducibility disclosure without calling it evidence of generalization, scientific validity, superiority, or a causal mechanism. If revised authoritative artifacts instead record failed qualification, disclose that failure throughout writing, review, audit, and revision while preserving all limitations; the cause remains unknown without diagnostics.\n+\n+The local final evaluator and evidence JSON hashes match the final metadata. The available constant-rate implementation specifies learning rate 0.01; its connection to the final evaluation is supported by retained source and campaign records, but an independently reconstructed match to the final program-tree hash has not been established. Keep this distinction explicit in the private audit. The source labels candidate diagnostics as unverified. The scientific observations used here are retained evaluator-generated traces, not candidate-reported measurements; do not extrapolate this into comprehensive integrity or adaptivity certification.\n+\n+### Actual Evaluated Setting\n+\n+- Modulus 97; addition and subtraction, not the proposal'\"'s alternate modulus or data fraction.\n+- Concatenated one-hot inputs and a linear–ReLU–linear network with hidden widths 16, 64, and 256; measured parameter counts 4769, 18785, and 74849.\n+- Full-batch cross-entropy training with AdamW, decay 0 or 1, the fixed constant-rate policy, and a 20,000-update horizon.\n+- Three initialization seeds: 1009, 2027, 3037. Each seed episode contains twelve condition records; do not call the three episodes three training runs or treat all 36 condition records as independent replications.\n+- Each operation's deterministic final pool contains 4705 pairs, split into 1411 training and 3294 held-out pairs. Splits are fixed across seeds. This is not 30% training on all 97-squared input pairs.\n+- Checkpoints every 500 updates. Memorization requires training accuracy at least 0.99 at three consecutive checkpoints; generalization uses held-out accuracy at least 0.95 over the same persistence rule. The event is dated to the first checkpoint of the qualifying triplet.\n+\n+Method provenance: hash-matched \"'`task/evaluate_final.py`, `task/resources/final/benchmark.json`, `task/requirements.txt`, and the retained constant-rate source. Scientific observations and deterministic summaries are grounded in `final.evidence.episodes`; named metrics use `final.metric.*`. Do not manufacture additional source identifiers for unregistered code files.\n+\n+## Scientific Explanation and Its Testability\n+\n+Use a deliberately limited accounting explanation: finite-horizon width differences in fitting can generate apparent lag differences even when no generalization time is observed. The stored event table tests the fitting part; the evaluator'\"'s exact formula tests the accounting part. This is a retrospective interpretation, not a preregistered mechanism test.\n+\n+The evidence gives 30 memorization events among 36 condition records and no sustained generalization event. Widths 64 and 256 memorize at checkpoint 500 in every condition. Width 16 without decay memorizes at checkpoint 1000 or 1500; width 16 with positive decay never meets the threshold. Checkpoint ties do not imply equal continuous-time dynamics.\n+\n+Let T be the training horizon, M the sustained memorization checkpoint, and G the sustained generalization checkpoint. The reported lag is T if M is absent; otherwise it is max(0, (G if observed else T) − M). When G is absent but M exists, this is the observed remaining follow-up after fitting, not an observed delay to generalization. When M is absent, a post-memorization delay is not even defined: T is a scoring convention.\n+\n+Under positive decay, width 16 receives T, whereas width 256 receives T−500. Their difference is therefore exactly 500 for every seed. The supplied interval [500, 500] reflects identical values of this capped statistic, not precise knowledge of latent grokking times. The reported decay interaction, 1083.3333333333335 updates, has the same limitation. Explain these facts in the body, not only the supplement.\n+\n+An observed generalization event or failure to reproduce this formula would defeat the present account of these stored contrasts. A causal explanation of why the networks do not generalize would require new interventions, which are out of scope here. The original claim about near-invariant true generalization times across width remains untested.\n+\n+## Included Method Groups\n+\n+1. **Fixed-rate width family without weight decay — baseline.** The within-evaluation reference, not the original lower-rate source program.\n+2. **Matched width family with unit decay — ablation.** The evaluated regularization contrast at the same widths, operations, seeds, and horizon; no claim of scale-matched initialization.\n+3. **Nonlearning prediction references — supporting.** Initial network, training-label mode, exact-pair lookup with mode fallback, and label-deranged-input predictions. Disjoint held-out pairs make the lookup and mode references identical. Derangement uses held-out labels to construct a diagnostic permutation and is not a deployable learned comparator or a random-label training experiment.\n+\n+Do not include proposal-only width grids, independent random-label networks, calibration procedures, mechanistic circuits, or a sequence of discarded scheduling branches as required methods.\n+\n+## Results Organization\n+\n+Both operations are condition-specific evidence for one thesis. Organize by scientific comparison, not by experiment order:\n+\n+1. **Width and Decay Effects on Fitting.** A twelve-row main event table shows each operation/decay/width condition, all three memorization times or non-attainment, and observed generalization count. Preserve the six narrow positive-decay fitting failures.\n+2. **Held-Out Outcomes.** Compare final-five-checkpoint training and held-out accuracy across width. Show the individual seed observations; contextualize held-out results using the available reference predictors. The stored per-record score is the final-five-checkpoint held-out mean, not an event-attainment rate.\n+3. **What the Capped Lag Measures.** Give the exact formula, the supplied contrast and degenerate interval, and the decay interaction with their identification caveats. These are comparisons over width, not learning-curve progression.\n+\n+If reporting the aggregate control gap, define it as the equally weighted late-window accuracy difference against four stored references, two of which coincide. Do not imply four independent controls. Avoid pooled significance tests, unsupported generalization-rate confidence intervals, or imputation of unobserved events as actual event times. Only three initialization seeds vary; neither dataset split nor operation supplies independent seed replication.\n+\n+## Required Figures and Readability\n+\n+The inspected ICLR template uses \"'`paper.sty`: **one 5.5-inch text column and a 9-inch text height**. A full-width figure is one text-column wide; do not assume a two-column conference format. All three required figures use the full text width. A nominal half-width figure would be only 2.75 inches wide and is inappropriate for these panel/annotation densities. Heights below are design budgets, not measured results.\n+\n+| Figure | Scientific content and generator | Budget and placement |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `study_overview` | One early design-and-inference overview using `generate-concept-figure`: the evaluated factorial, the two distinct event definitions, and the finite-horizon inference boundary. No fabricated curves or causal mechanisms. | Full width, page 1 or 2; 2 compartments, at most 2 across; at most 6 categories and 3 series per compartment; minimum 9-point rendered labels; graphic height about 1.7–2.0 inches plus caption. |\n+| `width_decay_outcomes` | Matplotlib seed dotplots. Columns: addition/subtraction. Rows: late-window training/held-out accuracy. Width on the horizontal axis, decay in two fixed colors, three seed markers and condition mean. | Full width; 4 panels in 2-by-2 layout; 3 width categories and 2 series per panel; minimum 8.5-point labels; graphic height about 3.1–3.5 inches plus caption. Match scales within rows; use separate row scales so held-out values remain visible. |\n+| `censoring_audit` | Matplotlib direct comparison of capped lag by width. One panel per decay condition; operation-specific neutral shapes/patterns and individual seeds. Explicitly mark missing memorization and state that generalization is unobserved throughout. | Full width; 2 panels in one row; 3 categories and 2 series per panel; minimum 9-point labels; graphic height about 2.0–2.3 inches plus caption. A labeled focused vertical range is acceptable; an apparent event at the cap is not. |\n+\n+Use one overview workflow only; orchestration, not this strategy stage, owns its execution. Keep Figure 2'\"'s decay colors semantically stable; Figure 3 can distinguish operations with neutral shapes rather than reassign those colors. No trajectory figure is required: direct outcomes and event tables support the thesis without a run diary or compressed learning curves.\n+\n+**Export contract.** Quantitative plots must have editable/reproducible plotting source, vector PDF, and 300-DPI PNG. Reference PDF from LaTeX whenever present. Require at least 2400 pixels for full-width raster output or 1200 for partial/column-width raster-only output. For a 5.5-inch final graphic, render the source canvas large enough to meet the PNG pixel budget with proportionally scaled typography, rather than upscaling a saved image. Preserve editable draw.io and any PDF export for the overview; use raster only if no PDF exists and meet the full-width pixel budget.\n+\n+## Body Layout and Scientific Value\n+\n+Target about **8.5 body pages**, excluding references and supplement, without margin or font changes. An eight-page body must finish at least 75% full under \"'`VENUE.md`.\n+\n+| Component | Approximate body-page allocation, figures included |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Abstract, Introduction, and early overview | 1.5 |\n+| Related Work | 0.75 |\n+| Experimental Design and Event Definitions | 1.75 |\n+| Results, both quantitative figures, and event table | 3.0 |\n+| Discussion and Limitations | 1.25 |\n+| Conclusion | 0.25 |\n+\n+Use the space for a precise fitting-versus-generalization question, exact event definitions, paired-seed evidence, readable comparisons, reference-predictor interpretation, the capped-lag derivation, and limits of identification. Do not fill pages with implementation history, repeated zero-event panels, literature padding, or unexecuted experiments. If the grounded material cannot fill the venue budget substantively, surface that conflict rather than disguise it.\n+\n+The template scaffold contains a named author and final-copy command; these are incompatible with anonymous review. The later writer must use anonymous review mode, omit author identities/affiliations/acknowledgements/funding and identifying links, preserve the required orchestrator watermark, and check ICLR 2026 submission compliance. The old style-file header alone does not establish latest-template provenance. Do not invent a venue checklist.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+Keep the decisive negative evidence and capped-lag limitation in the main paper. After the references, use the prescribed clear-page/appendix/Supplementary Information structure for:\n+\n+1. **Exact Data and Training Specification.** Deterministic data construction and final-pool counts; actual one-hot representation and network parameterization; optimizer settings; seed and checkpoint definitions. Source registry anchor: `final.evidence.episodes`, supplemented by the inspected final evaluator, resource JSON, and dependency file.\n+2. **Complete Condition-Level Observations.** All 36 records with events or non-attainment, capped lag, late-window accuracies, and completion. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.completion_fraction`, `final.metric.delayed_fraction`.\n+3. **Reference Predictors and Available Diagnostics.** Separate stored reference accuracies and the duplicate-control explanation; descriptive endpoint loss/norm tables only. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.control_gap`. No new mechanism test is implied by these diagnostics.\n+4. **Capped-Lag Calculation and Reproduction Map.** Exact event/aggregation pseudocode, three-seed paired contrast and Student-t interval construction, and artifact-to-script/table/figure mapping. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.restricted_mean_lag`, `final.metric.width_lag_contrast`, `final.metric.width_lag_ci_low`, `final.metric.width_lag_ci_high`, `final.metric.decay_interaction`. Document `numpy==2.1.3` and `torch==2.5.1+cpu`, and distinguish training from replotting stored results. The evaluator requires an RPC execution context; do not invent a working standalone command or undocumented hardware/runtime claim.\n+5. **LLM Usage.** A separate section discloses artifact-supported roles in idea proposal, bounded policy implementation, reference-query planning, framing, and writing, while distinguishing evaluator-owned training/measurements. Do not claim undocumented human review or model identities. Anchor to the final evidence and named local implementation/query-plan provenance; do not present an episode as sole proof of writing roles.\n+\n+Any subsequently supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses belong here by default. Do not guess their ranking, promote or discard them to satisfy page counts, or retroactively alter this strategy on that basis.\n+\n+## Limits, Reference Safety, and Writing Guardrails\n+\n+The empirical scope is one modulus, two related operations, one representation/architecture, three widths and three initialization seeds, a fixed split per operation, two decay values, one selected learning-rate recipe, and a finite horizon. Initialization scale is not matched across widths. There are no independently trained random-label controls, circuit measurements, or true generalization-time observations. Late threshold excursions without enough following checkpoints cannot meet the sustained-event rule. Non-attainment does not imply that grokking never occurs, and low accuracy alone does not identify the cause.\n+\n+Reference files contain retrieved metadata, including off-target entries; metadata retrieval is not proof of consultation. Only exact starter-literature identities verified against both bibliography and provenance may be used, and substantive claims require actually consulting the approved sources. Never identify a paper by a query-string match, expand citation graphs, or conduct broad width-grokking searches. This strategy made no external lookup and inspected local reference metadata only. Stop and log any identifiable prohibited encounter; do not infer the forbidden paper'\"'s identity. No novelty claim may depend on pretending that an unrestricted literature review was performed.\n+\n+**Forbidden headings:** Campaign Progression; Search Timeline; Milestones; First Successful Run; Phase 1 / Phase 2; Experiment A / Experiment B; Winning Configuration; Successive Improvements; Capacity-versus-Decay-Clock Mechanism Confirmed.\n+\n+**Forbidden public phrasing:** “we then tried,” “first valid result,” “subsequent improvements,” “next-best,” “later variants,” “search winner proves,” pipeline-native metric/acceptance labels listed in the JSON contract, “larger models grok faster,” “grokking never occurs,” “the confidence interval proves faster generalization,” claims of random-label control experiments, and “state of the art.” Internal field names and paths appear above only as private audit or source-routing instructions, not recommended manuscript language.\n+\n+Prefer explicit reader-facing names: memorization attainment, generalization attainment, late-window held-out accuracy, and administratively capped lag. Keep the two sustained thresholds distinct. A completed accepted evaluation is compatible with a scientifically negative observation; publication eligibility cannot upgrade that observation into evidence for a neural mechanism.\n+\n+## Stage Boundary\n+\n+Write only the strategy artifacts and append-only memory records in this stage. Do not draft \"'`paper.tex`, create `claims_grounding.json`, render figures, launch new experiments, or run final-paper validation. Validate the strategy'\"'s JSON structure, registered source IDs, figure budgets, and consistency with existing evidence only.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/home/agent-home/.codex/tmp/arg0/codex-arg01Wi7zG/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Memorization Without Observed Grokking Across MLP Widths\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"Within a fixed training horizon, how do hidden width and weight decay affect memorization and observed generalization in modular-arithmetic MLPs, and what can a censored width-lag contrast actually establish?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"Across the tested modular addition and subtraction conditions, wider fixed-rate MLPs attain sustained memorization earlier or attain it when the narrowest models do not, yet none attains sustained generalization within 20,000 updates; the reported width-lag contrast therefore reflects memorization and endpoint substitution, not an identified effect on grokking time.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The final evidence supports a controlled, finite-horizon negative-results study across width and decay, augmented by an exact audit of the reported lag statistic. This is stronger than a proposed capacity-versus-decay-clock mechanism, which lacks the proposed random-label and calibration interventions, or a learning-rate-superiority story, which lacks a final-plane comparator. The scientific contribution is the observed separation between fitting and generalization plus the identification limit of capped lag, not a new optimizer or a universal claim about model scale. The original mechanistic question is only partially answered. Negative results support a coherent standalone paper, but readiness is not a prediction of ICLR acceptance.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"Fresh framing rather than an edit: no previous_paper directory, resolved edit-context files, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory is present. The status recentered refers to replacing the source proposal's mechanistic ambition with the actually evaluated finite-horizon question; it does not imply that a prior manuscript existed. Preserve-proposal, broaden-to-annealing-family, and recenter-on-final-factorial framings were compared; the last has the strongest directly observed evidence.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"No staged old/new manuscript or implementation pair is available, so no inherited title, central question, or figure plan is retained by inertia.\\\",\n+    \\\"The hash-matched final evaluator fixes the actual setting: modulus 97, addition and subtraction, concatenated one-hot inputs, one-hidden-layer ReLU MLPs of widths 16, 64, and 256, full-batch AdamW, weight decay 0 or 1, and a 20,000-update horizon.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final evidence contains three seed episodes, each with twelve factorial condition records: 36 completed training records, 30 sustained memorization events, and zero sustained generalization events. These are deterministic summaries of final.evidence.episodes, not search outcomes.\\\",\n+    \\\"The available constant-rate implementation specifies learning rate 0.01. Its linkage to the final evaluation is supported by the retained implementation and campaign manifest; the final manifest supplies a program-tree hash but not an independently verified reconstructed source tree. Do not claim stronger file-level provenance than this.\\\",\n+    \\\"downstream_study is absent and there are no study.* grounding sources. Do not create a search-selection table, score-difference claim, or scored/unscored attempt accounting from memory or substitute result.* sources for a study contract.\\\",\n+    \\\"Final qualification is independently recorded as status completed, outcome qualified, and correct true by final.qualification.*. This does not establish scientific validity, adaptivity safeguards, superiority, or a grokking mechanism. Candidate diagnostic trust is labeled unverified; scientific observations here are the retained evaluator-generated traces, not candidate self-reports.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Fixed-rate MLP width family without weight decay\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Widths 16, 64, and 256 at the frozen constant-rate recipe supply the within-final-evaluation reference for fitting times and held-out behavior in both operations. This is a scientific reference condition, not an unevaluated original-program comparison.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Matched width family with unit weight decay\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The same widths, operation-specific data, seed values, training horizon, and learning-rate recipe with AdamW decay 1 isolate the evaluated decay intervention conditional on this architecture and initialization scheme. The narrowest networks never attain the memorization threshold, unlike widths 64 and 256.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Nonlearning prediction references\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Stored initial-network, training-label-mode, exact-pair lookup with mode fallback, and label-deranged-input prediction accuracies contextualize low held-out accuracy. The lookup and mode references coincide because held-out pairs are disjoint. These are not separately trained random-label networks and are not a causal mechanism test.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Lead with a width-by-decay comparison, split by addition and subtraction, rather than learning-rate search order. Use late-window training and held-out accuracy with individual seed observations; both operations are evidence blocks for one finite-horizon thesis, not separate discoveries.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep a main-text event table for all twelve operation/decay/width cells. Report all three observed memorization times or non-attainment, alongside generalization attainment counts. Widths 64 and 256 memorize at checkpoint 500 in every condition; width 16 without decay memorizes at 1000 or 1500; width 16 with decay never crosses. All 36 generalization events are unobserved.\\\",\n+    \\\"Define memorization as training accuracy at least 0.99 and generalization as held-out accuracy at least 0.95 at three consecutive checkpoints. Checkpoints are 500 updates apart; event times are the first checkpoint of a qualifying triplet, not precisely resolved continuous crossing times. Delayed generalization requires both observed events and a positive lag.\\\",\n+    \\\"Audit the capped-lag statistic explicitly. Its value is T when memorization is absent and max(0, (G if observed else T) - M) otherwise. For positive decay, the narrowest models receive T and width-256 models receive T-500, mechanically giving the reported 500-update contrast and [500, 500] interval. Report that interval faithfully as the supplied three-seed statistic, not as precision about unobserved generalization times.\\\",\n+    \\\"The supplied decay interaction of 1083.3333333333335 updates is also an interaction of the capped statistic, not evidence that decay changes a generalization clock. The negative no-decay width contrast follows earlier memorization in larger networks while generalization is absent. Keep the algebra and the censoring caveat in the main paper.\\\",\n+    \\\"Contextualize final held-out accuracy using stored nonlearning references. If the aggregate final accuracy or control gap is reported, define it in reader-facing units: the final-five-checkpoint mean and the equally weighted gap to four references, respectively. Do not treat the aggregate as superiority or compare it to search-plane aggregates.\\\",\n+    \\\"Show seed values rather than relying on significance tests. There are three independent initialization seeds on a fixed split per operation; the twelve condition records within a seed are paired, not twelve independent replications. Zero observed generalization does not identify eventual event rates or support a pooled independent-binomial confidence interval.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: the evaluated width-by-decay design, distinct memorization/generalization events, and the inference boundary imposed by a finite horizon. No invented learning curves or proposed unrun interventions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, main comparison: a 2-by-2 quantitative display of late-window training and held-out accuracy against width; columns are operations, rows are distinct accuracy metrics, colors encode decay, and seed points remain visible.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, censoring audit: two direct-comparison panels, one per decay condition, showing capped lag versus width with operation-specific series and individual seeds. Explicitly label every generalization time as unobserved and explain the endpoint-substitution identity next to the figure.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"study_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the evaluated factorial design and the difference between fitting, generalization, and censoring legible at a glance without asserting a neural mechanism.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"evaluated_factor_and_event_definition\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"not_applicable_design_schematic\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"design_and_inference_boundary\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected ICLR style has one 5.5-inch text column, not a two-column layout. Two adjacent schematic compartments need the entire 5.5-inch width; a nominal half-width rendering would be only 2.75 inches and force tiny labels. Target 1.7-2.0 inches of graphic height plus caption, about 0.3 body page, on page 1 or 2.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"minimum_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Left: addition/subtraction mod 97; three widths; decay 0/1; three seeds; one shared fixed-rate MLP protocol. Right: separate named memorization and generalization event definitions, the 20,000-update observation limit, and an explicit distinction between non-attainment and measured delay. Use grouping labels instead of twelve tiny condition boxes. Draw no synthetic trajectories, causal circuit arrows, or additional unperformed experiments.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"export_requirements\\\": \\\"Retain editable draw.io source and vector PDF export when available, plus a PNG generated at the required resolution. Reference the PDF in LaTeX whenever a PDF exists; if only raster survives, require at least 2400 pixels width, generated from source rather than upscaled.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"width_decay_outcomes\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Compare fitting and held-out behavior directly across widths and decay while displaying all seed-level uncertainty.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"faceted_seed_dotplot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"hidden_width\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"mean_accuracy_over_final_five_checkpoints\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"operation_and_accuracy_partition\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Four panels in two rows and two columns fit the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width at approximately 2.5 inches per panel after gutters. Target 3.1-3.5 inches graphic height plus caption, about 0.45 body page. Separate row scales prevent near-zero held-out values from disappearing under the training-accuracy range; scales match across operations within each row. Do not shrink a four-panel figure to half text width.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"minimum_rendered_font_pt\\\": 8.5,\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Columns: addition and subtraction. Top row: training accuracy averaged over each trace's last five checkpoints. Bottom row: held-out accuracy over that same window, matching each record's stored score. Plot widths 16, 64, 256 as categorical positions; use two consistent decay colors and three seed markers per condition with deterministic offsets. Show seed means without fabricated error bars. Do not label a single series as successful or reuse one threshold label across the two accuracy definitions. The main event table supplies sustained-threshold results.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"export_requirements\\\": \\\"Generate PDF and PNG from the same plotting script, PNG at 300 DPI and at least 2400 pixels wide; keep the PDF vector and reference it in LaTeX. Regenerate with appropriate source dimensions rather than upscaling a raster.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"censoring_audit\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose why a nonzero capped-lag width contrast is compatible with zero observed generalization events.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"faceted_capped_lag_dotplot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"hidden_width\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"administratively_capped_lag_in_updates\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"weight_decay\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Two side-by-side panels need the full 5.5-inch text width so capped observations, a shared legend, and the non-attainment annotation remain legible at 9-point text. Target 2.0-2.3 inches graphic height plus caption, about 0.3 body page. Use a visibly labeled focused vertical range covering the observed capped values; never imply a zero origin or an observed event at the cap.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"minimum_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Panels: decay 0 and decay 1. Two series encode operation using a separate, clearly labeled visual role from Figure 2's decay colors; prefer neutral operation-specific shapes/line patterns to avoid color reassignment. Draw each seed's capped lag and a condition mean. Distinguish missing memorization from observed memorization by fill or an explicit annotation. All generalization events are unobserved. Include the capped-lag formula in adjacent main text and report the 500-update contrast with its supplied degenerate interval there. Width is the horizontal axis, not search order or training progression.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_contrast\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.metric.decay_interaction\\\"],\n+      \\\"export_requirements\\\": \\\"Generate vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG from one script, PNG at least 2400 pixels wide. LaTeX must use the PDF whenever present. Preserve visible capped-data symbols and readable annotations at the final 5.5-inch width.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Provide an auditable condition-level record, exact data and training specification, and substantive reference-predictor and diagnostic detail without relocating the negative result or the censoring explanation out of the main paper.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Exact Data and Training Specification\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the actual modulus-97 dataset construction, deterministic operation-specific split, and final-plane pool: 4705 pairs per operation, 1411 training and 3294 held-out. Specify one-hot concatenation, linear-ReLU-linear architecture, parameter counts 4769/18785/74849, full-batch cross-entropy, AdamW defaults explicitly set by the evaluator, checkpoint cadence, constant learning-rate implementation, and seeds 1009/2027/3037. Architectural and split facts come from the hash-matched task/evaluate_final.py and task/resources/final/benchmark.json; episode records anchor the evaluated cases and measured parameter counts. Do not replace these with proposal-only settings.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Condition-Level Observations\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Give a 36-row seed/operation/decay/width table with memorization event or non-attainment, generalization non-attainment, capped lag, final-five-checkpoint training and held-out accuracy, and completion status. Retain every condition, including the six narrow positive-decay fitting failures and all zero generalization outcomes. The main paper retains the twelve-cell event summary and decisive comparisons.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.completion_fraction\\\", \\\"final.metric.delayed_fraction\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Reference Predictors and Available Diagnostics\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate each stored reference accuracy separately rather than only the aggregate control gap. Explain the duplicate lookup/mode reference and the held-out-label construction of the deranged-input diagnostic. Provide condition-level endpoint loss and weight-norm summaries from the existing traces only; mark them descriptive and avoid circuit, representation, or causal explanations. No new random-label training, calibration intervention, or norm ablation is implied.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_gap\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Capped-Lag Calculation and Reproduction Map\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Supply exact event and aggregation pseudocode from the hash-matched final evaluator, the paired-by-seed contrast calculation and its Student-t multiplier, derivations of every reported aggregate, and an artifact-to-script/table/figure map. Keep the central 500-update identity and its scientific limitation in the body. Reproduction instructions must distinguish training from replotting stored results, list numpy 2.1.3 and torch 2.5.1+cpu from task/requirements.txt, and describe the actual RPC dependency rather than inventing a standalone command. Omit unmeasured runtime estimates and unverified hardware claims.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.restricted_mean_lag\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_contrast\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.metric.decay_interaction\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the artifact-supported roles of LLMs in idea proposal, the bounded learning-rate implementation, reference-query planning, and paper framing/writing. Distinguish evaluator-owned neural training and measurements from generated prose and candidate proposals. State only observed roles; do not infer undocumented human review or model identities. Relevant implementation files and reference_query_plan.md provide provenance in addition to the final evidence record.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Campaign Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Search Timeline\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Successful Run\\\",\n+    \\\"Phase 1 / Phase 2\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Configuration\\\",\n+    \\\"Successive Improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"Capacity-versus-Decay-Clock Mechanism Confirmed\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"search winner proves\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"larger models grok faster\\\",\n+    \\\"grokking never occurs\\\",\n+    \\\"the confidence interval proves faster generalization\\\",\n+    \\\"random-label control experiments\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"PUBLIC OUTLINE AND PAGE PLAN: Target 8.5 body pages under VENUE.md, within its 8-9-page requirement and without changing the template geometry. Allocate approximately 1.5 pages to abstract/introduction and the early overview, 0.75 to related work, 1.75 to methods and event definitions, 3.0 to results including both quantitative figures and the twelve-cell event table, 1.25 to discussion/limitations, and 0.25 to conclusion. These are layout budgets, not measurements. Ensure an eight-page body ends at least 75% full. Use available space for the event/censoring derivation, transparent references, paired uncertainty, and scope analysis rather than additional weak claims. If this cannot fill the budget substantively, flag that conflict rather than add filler.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC SECTION PLAN: Introduction; Related Work; Experimental Design and Event Definitions; Results with Width and Decay Effects on Fitting, Held-Out Outcomes, and What the Capped Lag Measures; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. After references, begin Supplementary Information with the planned grounded subsections, including a separate LLM Usage section. No visible search chronology.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC HYPOTHESIS PLAN: Present the modest accounting explanation that finite-horizon width differences in fitting can generate apparent lag differences without observed differences in generalization. State testable implications for the stored event table and the exact capped-lag identity, and label this interpretation retrospective, not preregistered. The data support earlier fitting at larger widths but cannot test the original equivalence prediction about true generalization times, a capacity mechanism, or a decay-clock explanation. New generalization events or a failure of the identity would defeat the present account of these observed contrasts.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC UNCERTAINTY PLAN: Report individual initialization seeds, fixed data splits, pairing, and checkpoint resolution. A first sustained event requires a triplet, so late threshold excursions lacking two following observations cannot qualify. Administrative non-attainment is not evidence of permanent failure. Do not impute unobserved event times as actual times or fit a survival curve that purports to estimate an unseen generalization-time distribution. In narrow positive-decay cases, a post-memorization lag is undefined; the value T is a scoring convention.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC LIMITATIONS: One modulus, two related operations, one representation and one-hidden-layer architecture, three widths, three initializations, a fixed split per operation, only two decay values, one selected learning-rate recipe, no scale-matched initialization, no random-label training control, no mechanistic circuit measures, and a finite horizon. Checkpoint ties do not establish identical continuous-time dynamics. Decay changes the trained system; norms alone cannot attribute a mechanism. Original broader scientific predictions remain untested.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC REFERENCE PLAN: Use only exact starter-literature identities verified against references.bib and references_provenance.json and actually consulted before substantive citation. Retrieval provenance includes off-target metadata and is not itself evidence that a work was read. Do not use query-string matches as paper-identity verification, expand citation graphs, or search broadly for width-grokking work. Stop and log any identifiable prohibited encounter. No external retrieval was performed during strategy generation; this stage inspected local reference metadata only. Use established grokking/AdamW context without claiming novelty by absence of a literature search.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC TEMPLATE PLAN: The inspected templates/iclr/paper.tex and paper.sty are single-column, with textwidth 5.5 inches and textheight 9 inches. The scaffold contains a named author and a final-copy command inconsistent with the brief's anonymous submission; the writer must use anonymous review mode, omit author affiliations/acknowledgements/funding and identifying links, preserve the required orchestrator watermark, and not change margins or fonts. Inspect ICLR 2026 compliance and any required checklist without inventing a checklist or claiming that the old style-file header independently certifies latest-template provenance.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC FIGURE PLAN: All required figures are full text width in this single-column format. Create only one concept figure through the specified orchestrator workflow; do not invoke it during strategy generation. Plan vector-first quantitative figures and retain editable sources. Export quantitative PDFs plus 300-DPI PNGs; at 5.5-inch final placement, obtain the required 2400-pixel PNG width by rendering the source canvas sufficiently large with proportionally scaled typography, not by raster upscaling. Prefer PDF in LaTeX whenever available. Raster-only assets require at least 2400 pixels full width or 1200 pixels column/partial width. Keep every required figure within its panel, category, series, and font budgets.\\\",\n+    \\\"PUBLIC MAIN-TEXT TABLE PLAN: Include a compact twelve-row event table, grouped by operation and decay, with width, the three seed-specific memorization times or non-attainment, and observed generalization count. Separately summarize nonlearning-reference definitions and their equality where appropriate. Do not merge the 99% fitting threshold and 95% generalization threshold under an ambiguous successful-run label.\\\",\n+    \\\"PRIVATE-ONLY GROUNDING: Quantitative scientific sources are final.evidence.episodes and final.metric.*. Qualification must be read independently from final.qualification.status, final.qualification.outcome, and final.qualification.correct; current values are completed, qualified, and true. State the recorded evaluation outcome faithfully in the reproducibility disclosure as a completed evaluation accepted under its recorded criteria, while explicitly denying that acceptance certifies generalization or mechanism. If a revision changes the authoritative outcome to not_qualified, explicitly disclose failed qualification in the paper, review, audit, and revision; retain measurements with all limitations and do not diagnose performance, validity, or adaptivity failure without evaluator evidence. Missing gate diagnostics remain unknown. Keep pipeline-native field names and internal paths out of public prose.\\\",\n+    \\\"PRIVATE-ONLY SELECTION BOUNDARY: There is no downstream_study or study.* source namespace in this bundle. The implemented constant-rate policy is the studied fixed configuration, not a new inferred winner. The original source policy uses learning rate 0.001, but no comparable final-plane evaluation of it is retained; omit that empirical comparison rather than substitute search scores. Do not report search deltas, search winner claims, or scored/unscored attempt counts. Neither missing results nor discarded proposals are measured losses.\\\",\n+    \\\"PRIVATE-ONLY TRUST AND PROVENANCE: task/evaluate_final.py and ../final_evaluation/results/evaluation_evidence.json match the evaluator/evidence hashes in final metadata. The episode source is tagged candidate_diagnostics_trust unverified; it contains evaluator-generated training observations and must not be upgraded into a claim of comprehensive integrity/adaptivity certification. Supplement source_ids identify the existing episode registry entry; code and resource files named in grounded_content provide additional method provenance, not newly fabricated grounding IDs. No actual paper, figures, claim map, or final-paper validation should be produced in this strategy stage.\\\",\n+    \\\"SUPPLEMENT ROUTING: Keep the zero-generalization result, the narrow positive-decay fitting failure, all main event definitions, and the capped-lag caveat in the body. Place full seed tables, detailed data construction, predictor diagnostics, and reproduction mapping after references. Route any separately supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses to Supplementary Information without inventing rankings or modifying this strategy to guess them.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Strategy\n+\n+**Status:** ready for \"'`paper_standalone` using `write-paper-standalone`; strategy only, not a manuscript.\n+\n+**Provisional title:** Memorization Without Observed Grokking Across MLP Widths\n+\n+## Central Question and Thesis\n+\n+**Question.** Within a fixed training horizon, how do hidden width and weight decay affect memorization and observed generalization in modular-arithmetic MLPs, and what can a censored width-lag contrast actually establish?\n+\n+**Thesis.** Across the tested addition and subtraction conditions, wider fixed-rate MLPs attain sustained memorization earlier or attain it when the narrowest models do not. None attains sustained generalization within 20,000 updates. The reported width-lag contrast consequently reflects fitting and endpoint substitution, not an identified effect on grokking time.\n+\n+This is a finite-horizon negative-results paper with a metric-identification analysis, not a new scheduling algorithm or a demonstrated neural mechanism. Its strength is a clear separation between what the experiments observe and what their lag statistic cannot establish. It partially answers the original research question; it does not complete the original proposed mechanistic investigation. Readiness means a coherent grounded paper is possible, not that ICLR acceptance or a novelty claim has been established.\n+\n+## Evidence and Framing Decision\n+\n+No prior manuscript, resolved edit-context input, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` directory is present. The JSON status `recentered` describes a fresh shift from the source proposal to the observed scientific setting, not an edit to an existing paper. No inherited title or figure plan exists to preserve.\n+\n+Three framings were compared:\n+\n+| Candidate framing | Decision | Grounded reason |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Preserve the proposed capacity-versus-decay-clock explanation | Reject as the thesis | Random-label fitting controls, initial-logit calibration, and the proposed generalization-time equivalence test were not performed. |\n+| Broaden into an annealing or optimizer-method family | Reject as the thesis | A selected fixed recipe has final evidence, but alternate schedules and the original lower-rate implementation lack matched final-plane comparisons. Search scores cannot establish final superiority or a width mechanism. |\n+| Recenter on the final width-by-decay factorial and censoring boundary | Select | The final evaluator supplies all condition-level training traces and the event/aggregation definitions needed to explain the negative result and audit the lag contrast. |\n+\n+The final evidence is independent of the source proposals and recent memory. `downstream_study` is absent; no `study.*` grounding sources are supplied. Do not invent a campaign selection contract, search score differences, or scored/unscored attempt counts. Omit a comparison against the original learning-rate-0.001 implementation because no comparable final-plane result is retained. Missing performance evidence is not a loss.\n+\n+### Private Qualification and Provenance Audit\n+\n+The authoritative `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, and `final.qualification.correct` values are **completed**, **qualified**, and **true**, respectively. Do not replace these with an earlier search acceptance or failure label. Record the completed, accepted evaluation in a reader-facing reproducibility disclosure without calling it evidence of generalization, scientific validity, superiority, or a causal mechanism. If revised authoritative artifacts instead record failed qualification, disclose that failure throughout writing, review, audit, and revision while preserving all limitations; the cause remains unknown without diagnostics.\n+\n+The local final evaluator and evidence JSON hashes match the final metadata. The available constant-rate implementation specifies learning rate 0.01; its connection to the final evaluation is supported by retained source and campaign records, but an independently reconstructed match to the final program-tree hash has not been established. Keep this distinction explicit in the private audit. The source labels candidate diagnostics as unverified. The scientific observations used here are retained evaluator-generated traces, not candidate-reported measurements; do not extrapolate this into comprehensive integrity or adaptivity certification.\n+\n+### Actual Evaluated Setting\n+\n+- Modulus 97; addition and subtraction, not the proposal'\"'s alternate modulus or data fraction.\n+- Concatenated one-hot inputs and a linear–ReLU–linear network with hidden widths 16, 64, and 256; measured parameter counts 4769, 18785, and 74849.\n+- Full-batch cross-entropy training with AdamW, decay 0 or 1, the fixed constant-rate policy, and a 20,000-update horizon.\n+- Three initialization seeds: 1009, 2027, 3037. Each seed episode contains twelve condition records; do not call the three episodes three training runs or treat all 36 condition records as independent replications.\n+- Each operation's deterministic final pool contains 4705 pairs, split into 1411 training and 3294 held-out pairs. Splits are fixed across seeds. This is not 30% training on all 97-squared input pairs.\n+- Checkpoints every 500 updates. Memorization requires training accuracy at least 0.99 at three consecutive checkpoints; generalization uses held-out accuracy at least 0.95 over the same persistence rule. The event is dated to the first checkpoint of the qualifying triplet.\n+\n+Method provenance: hash-matched \"'`task/evaluate_final.py`, `task/resources/final/benchmark.json`, `task/requirements.txt`, and the retained constant-rate source. Scientific observations and deterministic summaries are grounded in `final.evidence.episodes`; named metrics use `final.metric.*`. Do not manufacture additional source identifiers for unregistered code files.\n+\n+## Scientific Explanation and Its Testability\n+\n+Use a deliberately limited accounting explanation: finite-horizon width differences in fitting can generate apparent lag differences even when no generalization time is observed. The stored event table tests the fitting part; the evaluator'\"'s exact formula tests the accounting part. This is a retrospective interpretation, not a preregistered mechanism test.\n+\n+The evidence gives 30 memorization events among 36 condition records and no sustained generalization event. Widths 64 and 256 memorize at checkpoint 500 in every condition. Width 16 without decay memorizes at checkpoint 1000 or 1500; width 16 with positive decay never meets the threshold. Checkpoint ties do not imply equal continuous-time dynamics.\n+\n+Let T be the training horizon, M the sustained memorization checkpoint, and G the sustained generalization checkpoint. The reported lag is T if M is absent; otherwise it is max(0, (G if observed else T) − M). When G is absent but M exists, this is the observed remaining follow-up after fitting, not an observed delay to generalization. When M is absent, a post-memorization delay is not even defined: T is a scoring convention.\n+\n+Under positive decay, width 16 receives T, whereas width 256 receives T−500. Their difference is therefore exactly 500 for every seed. The supplied interval [500, 500] reflects identical values of this capped statistic, not precise knowledge of latent grokking times. The reported decay interaction, 1083.3333333333335 updates, has the same limitation. Explain these facts in the body, not only the supplement.\n+\n+An observed generalization event or failure to reproduce this formula would defeat the present account of these stored contrasts. A causal explanation of why the networks do not generalize would require new interventions, which are out of scope here. The original claim about near-invariant true generalization times across width remains untested.\n+\n+## Included Method Groups\n+\n+1. **Fixed-rate width family without weight decay — baseline.** The within-evaluation reference, not the original lower-rate source program.\n+2. **Matched width family with unit decay — ablation.** The evaluated regularization contrast at the same widths, operations, seeds, and horizon; no claim of scale-matched initialization.\n+3. **Nonlearning prediction references — supporting.** Initial network, training-label mode, exact-pair lookup with mode fallback, and label-deranged-input predictions. Disjoint held-out pairs make the lookup and mode references identical. Derangement uses held-out labels to construct a diagnostic permutation and is not a deployable learned comparator or a random-label training experiment.\n+\n+Do not include proposal-only width grids, independent random-label networks, calibration procedures, mechanistic circuits, or a sequence of discarded scheduling branches as required methods.\n+\n+## Results Organization\n+\n+Both operations are condition-specific evidence for one thesis. Organize by scientific comparison, not by experiment order:\n+\n+1. **Width and Decay Effects on Fitting.** A twelve-row main event table shows each operation/decay/width condition, all three memorization times or non-attainment, and observed generalization count. Preserve the six narrow positive-decay fitting failures.\n+2. **Held-Out Outcomes.** Compare final-five-checkpoint training and held-out accuracy across width. Show the individual seed observations; contextualize held-out results using the available reference predictors. The stored per-record score is the final-five-checkpoint held-out mean, not an event-attainment rate.\n+3. **What the Capped Lag Measures.** Give the exact formula, the supplied contrast and degenerate interval, and the decay interaction with their identification caveats. These are comparisons over width, not learning-curve progression.\n+\n+If reporting the aggregate control gap, define it as the equally weighted late-window accuracy difference against four stored references, two of which coincide. Do not imply four independent controls. Avoid pooled significance tests, unsupported generalization-rate confidence intervals, or imputation of unobserved events as actual event times. Only three initialization seeds vary; neither dataset split nor operation supplies independent seed replication.\n+\n+## Required Figures and Readability\n+\n+The inspected ICLR template uses \"'`paper.sty`: **one 5.5-inch text column and a 9-inch text height**. A full-width figure is one text-column wide; do not assume a two-column conference format. All three required figures use the full text width. A nominal half-width figure would be only 2.75 inches wide and is inappropriate for these panel/annotation densities. Heights below are design budgets, not measured results.\n+\n+| Figure | Scientific content and generator | Budget and placement |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `study_overview` | One early design-and-inference overview using `generate-concept-figure`: the evaluated factorial, the two distinct event definitions, and the finite-horizon inference boundary. No fabricated curves or causal mechanisms. | Full width, page 1 or 2; 2 compartments, at most 2 across; at most 6 categories and 3 series per compartment; minimum 9-point rendered labels; graphic height about 1.7–2.0 inches plus caption. |\n+| `width_decay_outcomes` | Matplotlib seed dotplots. Columns: addition/subtraction. Rows: late-window training/held-out accuracy. Width on the horizontal axis, decay in two fixed colors, three seed markers and condition mean. | Full width; 4 panels in 2-by-2 layout; 3 width categories and 2 series per panel; minimum 8.5-point labels; graphic height about 3.1–3.5 inches plus caption. Match scales within rows; use separate row scales so held-out values remain visible. |\n+| `censoring_audit` | Matplotlib direct comparison of capped lag by width. One panel per decay condition; operation-specific neutral shapes/patterns and individual seeds. Explicitly mark missing memorization and state that generalization is unobserved throughout. | Full width; 2 panels in one row; 3 categories and 2 series per panel; minimum 9-point labels; graphic height about 2.0–2.3 inches plus caption. A labeled focused vertical range is acceptable; an apparent event at the cap is not. |\n+\n+Use one overview workflow only; orchestration, not this strategy stage, owns its execution. Keep Figure 2'\"'s decay colors semantically stable; Figure 3 can distinguish operations with neutral shapes rather than reassign those colors. No trajectory figure is required: direct outcomes and event tables support the thesis without a run diary or compressed learning curves.\n+\n+**Export contract.** Quantitative plots must have editable/reproducible plotting source, vector PDF, and 300-DPI PNG. Reference PDF from LaTeX whenever present. Require at least 2400 pixels for full-width raster output or 1200 for partial/column-width raster-only output. For a 5.5-inch final graphic, render the source canvas large enough to meet the PNG pixel budget with proportionally scaled typography, rather than upscaling a saved image. Preserve editable draw.io and any PDF export for the overview; use raster only if no PDF exists and meet the full-width pixel budget.\n+\n+## Body Layout and Scientific Value\n+\n+Target about **8.5 body pages**, excluding references and supplement, without margin or font changes. An eight-page body must finish at least 75% full under \"'`VENUE.md`.\n+\n+| Component | Approximate body-page allocation, figures included |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Abstract, Introduction, and early overview | 1.5 |\n+| Related Work | 0.75 |\n+| Experimental Design and Event Definitions | 1.75 |\n+| Results, both quantitative figures, and event table | 3.0 |\n+| Discussion and Limitations | 1.25 |\n+| Conclusion | 0.25 |\n+\n+Use the space for a precise fitting-versus-generalization question, exact event definitions, paired-seed evidence, readable comparisons, reference-predictor interpretation, the capped-lag derivation, and limits of identification. Do not fill pages with implementation history, repeated zero-event panels, literature padding, or unexecuted experiments. If the grounded material cannot fill the venue budget substantively, surface that conflict rather than disguise it.\n+\n+The template scaffold contains a named author and final-copy command; these are incompatible with anonymous review. The later writer must use anonymous review mode, omit author identities/affiliations/acknowledgements/funding and identifying links, preserve the required orchestrator watermark, and check ICLR 2026 submission compliance. The old style-file header alone does not establish latest-template provenance. Do not invent a venue checklist.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+Keep the decisive negative evidence and capped-lag limitation in the main paper. After the references, use the prescribed clear-page/appendix/Supplementary Information structure for:\n+\n+1. **Exact Data and Training Specification.** Deterministic data construction and final-pool counts; actual one-hot representation and network parameterization; optimizer settings; seed and checkpoint definitions. Source registry anchor: `final.evidence.episodes`, supplemented by the inspected final evaluator, resource JSON, and dependency file.\n+2. **Complete Condition-Level Observations.** All 36 records with events or non-attainment, capped lag, late-window accuracies, and completion. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.completion_fraction`, `final.metric.delayed_fraction`.\n+3. **Reference Predictors and Available Diagnostics.** Separate stored reference accuracies and the duplicate-control explanation; descriptive endpoint loss/norm tables only. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.control_gap`. No new mechanism test is implied by these diagnostics.\n+4. **Capped-Lag Calculation and Reproduction Map.** Exact event/aggregation pseudocode, three-seed paired contrast and Student-t interval construction, and artifact-to-script/table/figure mapping. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.restricted_mean_lag`, `final.metric.width_lag_contrast`, `final.metric.width_lag_ci_low`, `final.metric.width_lag_ci_high`, `final.metric.decay_interaction`. Document `numpy==2.1.3` and `torch==2.5.1+cpu`, and distinguish training from replotting stored results. The evaluator requires an RPC execution context; do not invent a working standalone command or undocumented hardware/runtime claim.\n+5. **LLM Usage.** A separate section discloses artifact-supported roles in idea proposal, bounded policy implementation, reference-query planning, framing, and writing, while distinguishing evaluator-owned training/measurements. Do not claim undocumented human review or model identities. Anchor to the final evidence and named local implementation/query-plan provenance; do not present an episode as sole proof of writing roles.\n+\n+Any subsequently supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses belong here by default. Do not guess their ranking, promote or discard them to satisfy page counts, or retroactively alter this strategy on that basis.\n+\n+## Limits, Reference Safety, and Writing Guardrails\n+\n+The empirical scope is one modulus, two related operations, one representation/architecture, three widths and three initialization seeds, a fixed split per operation, two decay values, one selected learning-rate recipe, and a finite horizon. Initialization scale is not matched across widths. There are no independently trained random-label controls, circuit measurements, or true generalization-time observations. Late threshold excursions without enough following checkpoints cannot meet the sustained-event rule. Non-attainment does not imply that grokking never occurs, and low accuracy alone does not identify the cause.\n+\n+Reference files contain retrieved metadata, including off-target entries; metadata retrieval is not proof of consultation. Only exact starter-literature identities verified against both bibliography and provenance may be used, and substantive claims require actually consulting the approved sources. Never identify a paper by a query-string match, expand citation graphs, or conduct broad width-grokking searches. This strategy made no external lookup and inspected local reference metadata only. Stop and log any identifiable prohibited encounter; do not infer the forbidden paper'\"'s identity. No novelty claim may depend on pretending that an unrestricted literature review was performed.\n+\n+**Forbidden headings:** Campaign Progression; Search Timeline; Milestones; First Successful Run; Phase 1 / Phase 2; Experiment A / Experiment B; Winning Configuration; Successive Improvements; Capacity-versus-Decay-Clock Mechanism Confirmed.\n+\n+**Forbidden public phrasing:** “we then tried,” “first valid result,” “subsequent improvements,” “next-best,” “later variants,” “search winner proves,” pipeline-native metric/acceptance labels listed in the JSON contract, “larger models grok faster,” “grokking never occurs,” “the confidence interval proves faster generalization,” claims of random-label control experiments, and “state of the art.” Internal field names and paths appear above only as private audit or source-routing instructions, not recommended manuscript language.\n+\n+Prefer explicit reader-facing names: memorization attainment, generalization attainment, late-window held-out accuracy, and administratively capped lag. Keep the two sustained thresholds distinct. A completed accepted evaluation is compatible with a scientifically negative observation; publication eligibility cannot upgrade that observation into evidence for a neural mechanism.\n+\n+## Stage Boundary\n+\n+Write only the strategy artifacts and append-only memory records in this stage. Do not draft \"'`paper.tex`, create `claims_grounding.json`, render figures, launch new experiments, or run final-paper validation. Validate the strategy'\"'s JSON structure, registered source IDs, figure budgets, and consistency with existing evidence only.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\"","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA paper_strategy.json\nA paper_strategy.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
